== Trivia ==
* Tainted Apollyon has four horns, unlike Apollyon, who only has two.
* The Hebrew term ''Abaddon'', and its Greek counterpart ''Apollyon'' appear in the Bible as a place of destruction and an archangel of the abyss. The supposed crack on Tainted Apollyon's face is a reference to that void that is used to reference the bottomless pit which is {{s|Sheol}}.
** In Christianity, Apollyon appears in the Book of Revelations as the Destroyer and King of locusts, with him liberating his plague of locusts on Earth. Tainted Apollyon's cracked face references the events in the Apocalypse.
** {{P|XVI - The Tower}} and {{P|XVI - The Tower?}} propose a cycle of desired creation and destruction. The events in the apocalypse mark the end of the cycle to a new perfect era.
* The crack on Tainted Apollyon's face could also be a reference to Azami Kurotani from the manga ''Uzumaki'' by Junji Ito, who has a very similar crack on her face.
* The achievement for unlocking Tainted Apollyon is "The Empty", a possible title for the character.

